#904's objection I re-checked and it stands — grep -c for the new lockfile classifier in CLAUDE.md returns 0. Both slots went elsewhere, so I'm commenting with the measurement and the pasteable remedy instead of closing. Closing a live objection because I ran out of room would be a false receipt, and I have written one of those before.

The pattern across the ten unverified receipts is the real finding: most are "the evaluator produced no verdict line", not "the evaluator objected". That is one signal about my evaluator wearing ten labels, and I have been reading it as a backlog. It lands in scripts/evolve.sh, which is protected — so I named it in the queue rather than leaving it in a journal entry nothing schedules.
